1
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:10,200
Hello.

2
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:21,320
How nice.
We would be gathered here to talk about the coming legislation-

3
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:25,240
-And what it can mean for you who work locally.

4
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:31,760
The reason we have this session, it is both to capture the ER-

5
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:37,280
-It's the beginning of a needs inventory of how we should design our support to ER-

6
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:42,600
-If the future legislation.
It's a way for us to start ...

7
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:45,400
"This is what we think."

8
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:51,240
You can give feedback.
How right do you think we end up in our discussions?

9
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:55,600
Before we start, I'll introduce ourselves on stage.

10
00:00:55,680 --> 00:01:00,200
My name is Charlotta Gustafsson, I am from the Crime Prevention Council.

11
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:54,200
I thought we were doing a short recap on the law, which is proposed.

12
00:01:55,360 --> 00:02:00,560
There maybe Greta, Håkan and Malin want to fill up, but I'm starting a bit.

13
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:07,400
The law does not describe what a municipality should do, but more how a municipality should work.

14
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:12,000
It is both a strength and a weakness so clearly.

15
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:18,480
What you print a lot in the bill is that you have to work knowledge -based.

16
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:23,440
There should be a situation picture, which includes both a survey-

17
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:29,200
-A causal analysis and an information about the conditions one has-

18
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:31,680
-To prevent crime.

19
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:39,200
Based on the situation, one should formulate-

20
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:43,680
-The action plan, ie how to work with the questions-

21
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:50,200
-And after every two years do a follow -up of the work.

22
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:45,000
-Have I missed something?
-No.
I can say briefly too ...

23
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:49,600
... that the information I have received from Justitie and Skr-

24
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:54,080
— will the Law Council's remit be ready before the election-

25
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:57,720
-And the bill will be completed after the election.

26
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:03,600
The law is expected to enter into force on July 1, 2023, for those who do not know.

27
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:10,720
As Morgan said this morning, there is quite a great agreement around this law.

28
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:15,080
-Over party borders.
-Yes exactly.

29
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:20,320
Should we start by looking at how you have answered ...

30
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:23,920
Are you with us, Lars?

31
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,200
... on the survey.

32
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:30,720
So far you had answered ...

33
00:11:55,400 --> 00:12:01,000
The support that Brå and also the county administrative boards and the police provide to the municipalities-

34
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:06,280
-would be able to develop.
So you can develop the crime prevention work.

35
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:09,440
We have been negative to a legislation-

36
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:14,040
-But it is because we do not like the state controlling the municipalities.

37
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:17,480
It is more of such a aspect that we put in it.

38
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:21,160
Now we understand that we do not escape legislation.

39
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:27,360
Then it is more about how the state actors should support the municipalities-

40
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:30,720
-And what money will we get for this?

41
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:36,040
These are the issues we are now running.
From a crime prevention perspective-

42
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:41,200
-Can it have an effect, and you can get a mandate for the questions in a different way.

43
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:45,200
The municipalities are obliged to work with this.

44
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:33,120
Getting this as uniform as possible.
That we work in the same way in the country.

45
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:38,560
I think we have to safeguard municipal self -government.

46
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:45,480
We develop the crime prevention work by based on local conditions.

47
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:52,200
Speaking of local conditions, we have received a question where one wonders-

48
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:57,120
-If we can explain more what we mean by knowledge -based.

49
00:14:57,200 --> 00:15:04,160
We say the situation that includes survey, causal analysis.

50
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:10,120
"Have you had thoughts about the situation image as a basis for priorities"-

51
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:15,360
-"Out of what should be included? Is it a difference it would be good to have it explained."

52
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:20,320
From how we previously talked about situation pictures and what is in the legislation.

53
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:25,840
If there is a difference.
There is someone who says: "Good, Greta."

54
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:30,800
I'm just trying to be your speech tube.

55
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:37,840
-Do you want to answer the question?
-It's clear you should check the difficult.

56
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:43,240
Actually, there is not much difference to what is in the law text.

57
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:49,000
We have said that a situation picture should contain a survey and an analysis.

58
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:55,600
Then we have not quite as clearly talked about inventing their conditions-

59
00:15:55,680 --> 00:16:00,600
-Working crime prevention.
I don't know if you can see the spin in front of you.

60
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:03,880
That it says "initiate collaboration" at the top.

61
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:08,840
But one has to identify what it looks like organizationally to us.

62
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:13,720
What are we doing now?
What kind of structures do we have?
What can we use?

63
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:08,120
-With such information, and I think that is important.

64
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:14,720
I believe that if we get this base-

65
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:21,000
-when the legislation approaches, then the idea is that the work we put there-

66
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:27,480
-Do lead to something better than what we have done before, to the right action.

67
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:31,400
That is the very purpose of this.
The purpose is not collaboration-

68
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:38,240
-The position pictures or mapping.
The purpose is to get one step further through the tools.

69
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:43,000
It takes time.
Many of us here in the room have been doing this for years.

70
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:48,800
My hope is that we will be able to take the step and get a little better.

71
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:54,200
Get a little sharper, put in a little better action against what is actually the problem.

72
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:59,120
The collaboration for the sake of collaboration is meaningless.

73
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:04,400
We must never forget why we do this.
Not to get the complete position image-

74
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:59,800
-A of the crime prevention work.

75
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:06,840
We see how other types of crime categories are starting to become more and more interesting-

76
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:09,240
-At national level.

77
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:14,880
It is about environmental crime, it is about men's violence against women, the business issue.

78
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:20,000
Very interesting in relation to the crime prevention work-

79
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:26,920
-But also violation of welfare.
This clarifies the complexity-

80
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:33,040
-In the crime prevention work.
The new bill presses a little neighbor.

81
00:20:33,120 --> 00:20:39,480
Where you really show the importance of the entire municipality working crime prevention.

82
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:44,400
Many administrations have to enter this work and can contribute in a good way.

83
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:47,800
Both in a mode of image work-

84
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:52,840
-But also linked to solving the crime problems.

85
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:59,720
Cause analysis means to dive deep into a problem.

86
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:03,320
How can it be part of a situation picture?

87
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:08,320
I would like to say that a situation can ...

88
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:12,080
The survey will cover everything you have found.

89
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:17,080
But in the situation picture you also try to identify more as pattern-

90
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:20,480
-and make a compilation of their survey.

91
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:24,280
This means that you can prioritize certain crimes.

92
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:28,400
"This is what we want to know more about and do causal analysis about."

93
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:31,680
We do not say that one should do a causal analysis of all-

94
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:36,440
-An if you can report a survey that has covered a lot.

95
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:42,440
In this way, I think that the causal analysis will be included in the position image.

96
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:46,880
I hope I do not say to what we have written in the book.

97
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:53,120
Based on the situation, it is assumed that the collaborative parties-

98
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:58,200
-which is identified in this legislation, make its prioritization first-

99
00:21:58,280 --> 00:22:03,120
-When which are our most important problems we see?

100
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:39,360
-And how the municipalities work according to it.
We will follow up on it-

101
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:44,000
-And I suspect it will be like the annual report we do today.

102
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:50,400
It may be a bit like open comparisons, which Skr develops.

103
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:54,000
That you describe how the municipalities work.

104
00:24:54,080 --> 00:24:58,800
But we have no sanctioning authority.
We are not such an authority.

105
00:24:58,880 --> 00:25:02,080
We will only compile this.

106
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:09,000
There is no sanction, and it thinks that Skr is good.

107
00:25:09,080 --> 00:25:14,440
We also do not think that the state should control exactly what the municipality does-

108
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:17,440
-Or I think the municipalities want to do right.

109
00:25:17,520 --> 00:25:21,880
The municipalities want to work as well as they can in the crime prevention work.

110
00:25:21,960 --> 00:25:24,560
Then these must be anchored from above.

111
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:12,680
Not MD the priority that the security and security issues have in the municipalities.

112
00:26:12,760 --> 00:26:19,720
Fifteen years ago, these issues were not on the agenda as they are today.

113
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:22,800
Now almost all municipalities talk about this.

114
00:26:22,880 --> 00:26:29,680
Then you prioritize it differently, depending on what the crime looks like in the municipality.

115
00:26:29,760 --> 00:26:33,120
It will be a cue in to the next question.

116
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:40,160
We have received a question.
It is in itself good with national unity and structure-

117
00:26:40,240 --> 00:26:46,000
-But are there any thoughts with us about how to support the smaller municipalities?

118
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:51,440
They often have small resources and limited presence of police.

119
00:26:51,520 --> 00:26:57,360
In the bill, the county administrative boards also have ...

120
00:26:57,440 --> 00:27:04,120
It states that we must be allocated funds to provide operational support to municipalities-

121
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:08,720
-To reach the requirements of the legislation.

122
00:29:18,800 --> 00:29:21,080
-When we talk support.

123
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:25,760
There I can fill up, in the annual report I talked about earlier in day-

124
00:29:25,840 --> 00:29:27,760
-That we see a development-

125
00:29:27,840 --> 00:29:32,920
-There of metropolitan municipalities since 2017 have been high and stable.

126
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:37,280
They have fairly good conditions organizationally to work with the questions.

127
00:29:37,360 --> 00:29:43,400
They have a habit of doing mapping, causal analysis and follow -ups.

128
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:49,680
Then we have also followed the smaller municipalities, which we will support.

129
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:55,640
You can see that the curve is going up now.

130
00:29:55,720 --> 00:30:01,160
There are more people who have local advice.
More who have collaboration agreements.

131
00:30:01,240 --> 00:30:07,000
Smaller municipalities may not allocate a full-time service to this question-

132
00:30:07,080 --> 00:30:10,800
-Thaly combines it with several other prevention issues.

133
00:30:10,880 --> 00:30:15,800
You may not have had a pure education for the questions either.

134
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:20,000
Despite this, you still do surveys.
It goes up.

135
00:30:20,080 --> 00:30:26,400
It is more causal analysis, a little weaker with follow -up, but it is a positive trend.

136
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:29,960
But you look at the medium-sized municipalities-

137
00:30:30,040 --> 00:30:35,000
-When we barely talk about, but that are still quite a few in Sweden-

138
00:30:35,080 --> 00:30:39,000
-The their curve is more flat.

139
00:30:39,080 --> 00:30:45,000
In some respects, it has now begun to go down.

140
00:30:45,080 --> 00:30:49,480
When we said we need to look over all the municipalities-

141
00:30:49,560 --> 00:30:55,160
-blie the "big city, socially vulnerable areas, gang crime"--

142
00:30:55,240 --> 00:31:02,000
-Or it will be sparsely populated, and so we have lost middle milk Sweden.

143
00:31:04,360 --> 00:31:07,600
It may be coincidences that make it flicker out.

144
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:11,800
It can be a result after the restrictions of Covid-19.

145
00:31:11,880 --> 00:31:17,960
But we have to keep extra eyes to the medium -sized municipalities.

146
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:25,120
The county administrative boards' regional crime prevention coordinator-

147
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:28,000
-Find out throughout the country.

148
00:31:28,080 --> 00:31:33,000
We adapt our work based on the needs that exist in our county.

149
00:31:33,080 --> 00:31:39,400
That communication is important.
Contact the coordinator on the county administrative board.

150
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:45,000
Have a dialogue about what support you want, what support the county administrative board can provide.

151
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:50,080
It is also a way for us that, just as Lotta talked about earlier in day-

152
00:31:50,160 --> 00:31:54,280
-Being able to bring up the local level on a national level.

153
00:31:54,360 --> 00:31:59,080
Then we have to get it to us in order to pass it on.

154
00:33:06,280 --> 00:33:09,760
No, exactly.
This is a collaboration-

155
00:33:09,840 --> 00:33:14,160
-Which is to be based on agreeing on what to work with.

156
00:33:14,240 --> 00:33:16,240
Then you have to file on ...

157
00:33:16,320 --> 00:33:23,280
After all, there are municipalities that do not want to be part of the citizen promises-

158
00:33:23,360 --> 00:33:27,880
-like the police.
Municipalities have broken the cooperation agreement-

159
00:33:27,960 --> 00:33:31,560
-To you are dissatisfied with the police's representation.

160
00:33:31,640 --> 00:33:36,720
Then you have to try to find ... The very basis of the agreement-

161
00:33:36,800 --> 00:33:40,480
-Is, as Charlotta says, a kind of will.

162
00:33:40,560 --> 00:33:44,480
If one cannot agree on one point, it cannot be included in the agreement.

163
00:33:44,560 --> 00:33:48,240
If one is dissatisfied with the police presence-

164
00:33:48,320 --> 00:33:52,920
-Do not regulate the agreement.

165
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:59,440
What we can do better together in this work, we will work with that.

166
00:33:59,520 --> 00:34:05,360
Hopefully, in a collaboration, one can agree-

167
00:34:05,440 --> 00:34:08,760
-What to be included in the agreement, and not.

168
00:34:08,840 --> 00:34:12,400
If you cannot agree on a particular issue, you should not bring it.

169
00:34:12,480 --> 00:34:17,520
Neither the municipality nor the police can force the other to sign an agreement.

170
00:34:40,560 --> 00:34:47,400
The important thing is to have this collaboration and that you try to move on.

171
00:34:47,480 --> 00:34:54,320
Then you have to take a new hold the next time you negotiate or sit down and plan.

172
00:34:54,400 --> 00:35:00,720
Hopefully it is not a document that you hit the other in your head.

173
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:06,800
It should be a common will, which controls the work forward.

174
00:35:06,880 --> 00:35:09,440
We should be a little better together.

175
00:35:09,520 --> 00:35:15,360
It should not be a bat, a threat or a bribe.
That is not the purpose.

176
00:35:15,440 --> 00:35:21,440
The purpose is for us to get better.
That the municipality and police find the right measures.

177
00:35:21,520 --> 00:35:27,640
The police will take into account the municipality's picture of reality and vice versa.

178
00:35:27,720 --> 00:35:31,920
It's a hard question-

179
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:37,440
-But the very purpose is not to have it as a bat.

180
00:35:37,520 --> 00:35:41,400
We can't force anyone else, simply.

181
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:46,120
Before I give you the word I want to say, good Malin!

182
00:35:46,200 --> 00:35:51,000
-1-1.
-Now it's me zeroing.

183
00:35:51,080 --> 00:35:57,520
"Do you do the homework according to the book 'Collaboration in local crime prevention work'"-

184
00:35:57,600 --> 00:36:03,400
-Harms the agreement at the level that both parties have the opportunity to work with.

185
00:37:06,800 --> 00:37:11,480
-But also many police officers who are dissatisfied with the municipality.

186
00:37:11,560 --> 00:37:16,800
It looks very different, who is drawing in this work.

187
00:37:16,880 --> 00:37:18,840
What becomes more equal is-

188
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:24,720
-This is that both the police and the municipality have a crime prevention assignment by law.

189
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:29,040
That's the difference now.
Previously, the police have had the mission-

190
00:37:29,120 --> 00:37:36,080
-And the municipalities have been involved to the extent that they want or need.

191
00:37:36,160 --> 00:37:40,080
Now it becomes a kind of minimum requirement.
Both have the assignment.

192
00:37:40,160 --> 00:37:46,920
It may be able to help us get this balance that both parties weigh just as heavily.

193
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:53,640
It is very important in collaboration, that it is not the one or the other who has the power.

194
00:37:53,720 --> 00:37:57,040
The police should not dictate the conditions for the municipality.

195
00:37:57,120 --> 00:38:04,040
There are two equivalent parties who will agree and work towards a common goal.

196
00:41:09,720 --> 00:41:16,080
So it's longed for this.
We promise that we will stand up for.

197
00:41:16,160 --> 00:41:19,360
-Bra, Håkan.
-Yes.
Good, Håkan.

198
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:25,200
All you municipalities that have received these indications, this is a fellow

199
00:41:25,280 --> 00:41:30,600
-That police legislation does not change.
They are responsible for this question-

200
00:41:30,680 --> 00:41:33,880
-No like we will get it in the municipality.

201
00:41:33,960 --> 00:41:38,520
You have to take it into consideration, and then you have to have Håkan's words in the back-

202
00:41:38,600 --> 00:41:44,440
-That it's a joint job.
The police should not reverse, but take a step forward.

203
00:41:44,520 --> 00:41:49,520
There you have to be a little responsive to the way the situation looks out-

204
00:41:49,600 --> 00:41:55,720
-And you get to talk to your police locally, and what you have expectations.

205
00:41:55,800 --> 00:42:02,000
We have talked a lot on the county administrative boards.
What we get from the municipalities-

206
00:42:02,080 --> 00:42:07,120
-The coupled to the police, is very much about ...

207
00:42:07,200 --> 00:42:11,840
We believe that there will be greater demands on collaboration with the police.

208
00:42:11,920 --> 00:42:16,720
The municipalities will demand it, more will demand it.

209
00:42:16,800 --> 00:42:23,120
Part of it will be about the statistics, getting statistics from the police.

210
00:42:23,200 --> 00:42:28,200
That police officers should feel comfortable with what statistics they can disclose.

211
00:42:28,280 --> 00:42:34,280
It is a dialogue we have had long before this bill came too.

212
00:42:34,360 --> 00:42:38,640
There, the police are very clear about "that we should get it".

213
00:42:38,720 --> 00:42:42,120
There should be a clarity around it.

214
00:51:02,160 --> 00:51:06,320
It is that all municipalities say they need support-

215
00:51:06,400 --> 00:51:11,120
-But it looks very different what kind of support you need.

216
00:51:11,200 --> 00:51:15,720
This is what will be the challenge for us at national level-

217
00:51:15,800 --> 00:51:19,000
-Finding the right level of support.

218
00:51:19,080 --> 00:51:24,200
I think the county administrative boards will play a big role in this.

219
00:51:24,280 --> 00:51:28,920
One municipality in one county may need one type of support, another municipality another.

220
00:51:29,000 --> 00:51:34,840
Then you have to be responsive to it and adapt it to the needs that exist.

221
00:51:34,920 --> 00:51:41,440
I think there are different levels, but also in different ways at the different levels.

222
00:51:41,520 --> 00:51:48,480
Everyone does not say "we need support with mapping or training".

223
00:51:48,560 --> 00:51:51,280
It looks very different.

224
00:51:51,360 --> 00:51:54,120
The municipality's work looks very different.

225
00:51:54,200 --> 00:52:00,480
It reflects the multifaceted work that is to be based on the local problem picture.

226
00:52:00,560 --> 00:52:04,480
That it looks different, and that we work in different ways-

227
00:52:04,560 --> 00:52:11,000
-But that the common should be the structure and that we can achieve success.

228
00:55:19,320 --> 00:55:23,560
-To support your local crime prevention.
They exist, as well.

229
00:55:23,640 --> 00:55:27,680
We have a tradition of working with that and we are pretty good at that.

230
00:55:27,760 --> 00:55:31,560
We need to bring politicians and managers on this-

231
00:55:31,640 --> 00:55:35,720
-and that they understand what the law will mean.

232
00:55:35,800 --> 00:55:40,480
What does it mean to give an assignment to reach to produce a position image-

233
00:55:40,560 --> 00:55:46,320
-So that they really understand what they order and allocate resources in relation to it.

234
00:55:46,400 --> 00:55:52,120
I want to make a little bet that Brå is now, together with the county administrative boards-

235
00:55:52,200 --> 00:55:55,000
-even SKR and the police are involved on a corner-

236
00:55:55,080 --> 00:55:59,200
-Developing an education for managers and politicians.

237
00:55:59,280 --> 00:56:04,160
We feel that there is a strong need to clarify this.

238
00:56:04,240 --> 00:56:10,280
Someone has written in the chat and wants to tip about a course at Linnaeus University-

239
00:56:10,360 --> 00:56:14,280
-which is called "Crime prevention methods and collaboration".

240
00:56:14,360 --> 00:56:19,080
That training is open to police, municipality and county administrative boards-

241
00:58:41,320 --> 00:58:47,400
Many of the things come again.
Any thoughts about it?

242
00:58:48,960 --> 00:58:54,720
Many of the fears are interesting, and you have to try to work with it.

243
00:58:54,800 --> 00:58:57,320
But I think too-

244
00:58:57,400 --> 00:59:02,040
-That most municipalities want to do right.

245
00:59:02,120 --> 00:59:05,440
I usually try to say that to the county administrative board-

246
00:59:05,520 --> 00:59:10,000
-When sometimes think the municipalities are trying to throw away.

247
00:59:10,080 --> 00:59:14,680
"The municipalities do not want to throw away. They want to do right for themselves."

248
00:59:14,760 --> 00:59:17,880
This is no exception.

249
00:59:17,960 --> 00:59:22,000
I think you will do after best

250
00:59:22,080 --> 00:59:27,000
-To work this way and work forward on this issue.

251
00:59:27,080 --> 00:59:33,880
We should not get stuck in the legislation.
It becomes in some way like a wall.

252
00:59:33,960 --> 00:59:39,000
The idea is that we should be behind the legislation.
Move on to work.

253
01:01:00,800 --> 01:01:03,400
-Where it doesn't already exist today.

254
01:01:03,480 --> 01:01:07,200
I think we have to bring with us ... If you look at how far we have come-

255
01:01:07,280 --> 01:01:11,120
-In the crime prevention work, without legislation-

256
01:01:11,200 --> 01:01:16,560
-As by having produced support and having a crime prevention counsel-

257
01:01:16,640 --> 01:01:19,480
-And how far we have come.
Almost all municipalities in the day-

258
01:01:19,560 --> 01:01:22,920
-Have some type of cooperation supervision.
We do some type of survey.

259
01:01:23,000 --> 01:01:27,720
We do a lot of work that is in the right path.

260
01:01:27,800 --> 01:01:32,400
We have achieved this without legislation.

261
01:01:32,480 --> 01:01:36,080
We must have that with us - that we do this.

262
01:01:36,160 --> 01:01:39,360
This is not difficulty for us, we have done this before.
We know this.

263
01:01:39,440 --> 01:01:44,520
There is a lot of support to get and the state wants us to do this now.

264
01:03:34,040 --> 01:03:38,600
That's not how it's intended.
This is an indication of where we are going.

265
01:03:38,680 --> 01:03:43,800
If you have not come all the way then, I do not think it is the whole world.

266
01:03:43,880 --> 01:03:49,440
It is a work that we have to build on.
They should be better, year by year.

267
01:03:49,520 --> 01:03:52,840
That's the idea.
Even though the law says a certain level-

268
01:03:52,920 --> 01:03:55,440
-We can develop the work.

269
01:03:55,520 --> 01:03:58,400
-An better transition.
-Right?

270
01:03:58,480 --> 01:04:02,080
Then we have the last question we asked in the survey:

271
01:04:02,160 --> 01:04:06,120
"What will be better thanks to the law?"

272
01:04:06,200 --> 01:04:08,120
Just.

273
01:04:08,200 --> 01:04:13,560
There I think we could see two slightly larger areas.

274
01:04:13,640 --> 01:04:19,840
Partly it is about this work with bf-
